   "text": {
    "L1": "A 4-digit number has four places: thousands, hundreds, tens and ones.",
    "L2": "A digit's value depends on its place. In 3456, the 3 is worth 3000.",
    "L3": "We write a number by filling each place, not by joining the spoken parts.",
    "L4": "Here is a common mistake: leaving out the zero in four thousand fifty.",
    "L5": "The zero holds the empty hundreds place, so four thousand fifty is 4050.",
    "L6": "To write six thousand forty-two, make four places first.",
    "L7": "Put 6 thousands, 0 hundreds, 4 tens and 2 ones. The number is 6042.",
    "L8": "Now check: which number correctly shows four thousand fifty?"
   },
